  "answer": "Yes, this has been reported: PowerToys' Backup & restore does not include Command Palette settings (#43161). Changing Command Palette settings isn't even detected as a change, so PowerToys may say no new backup is needed. The tickets show no built-in fix yet, so please add your thumbs-up to #43161. In the meantime, back up Command Palette manually by copying its settings folder, which holds files such as bookmarks.json. It is usually at C:\\Users\\<you>\\AppData\\Local\\Packages\\Microsoft.CommandPalette_8wekyb3d8bbwe\\LocalState (hidden by default; for some installs, look under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Microsoft.CmdPal). Copy that folder to the new machine or after a reinstall to restore your settings."
 },
